@startuml
title Defense Core — Accepted Component View
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Workflow operator" as Operator
component "Browser / static UI" as Browser <<presentation>>

node "One FastAPI application process" as App {
  component "FastAPI boundary" as Boundary <<presentation>>
  component "Application services" as Services <<application>>
  component "Definition validator" as Validator <<domain>>
  component "Shared transition resolver\nand retry / terminal policy" as Resolver <<domain>>
  component "Centralized\norchestration strategy" as Orchestration <<application>>
  component "Choreography strategy" as Choreography <<application>>
  component "Run-scoped in-memory\nEventBus" as EventBus <<infrastructure>>
  component "Named deterministic\nscenario provider" as Scenario <<infrastructure>>
  component "Persistence boundary" as Persistence <<infrastructure>>
}

database "Persistent database / storage" as Database

Operator --> Browser : define/select, run, inspect
Browser --> Boundary : client requests
Boundary --> Services : use-case request
Services --> Validator : validate before run creation
Services --> Orchestration : select mode
Services --> Choreography : select mode
Orchestration --> Resolver : shared semantics
Choreography --> Resolver : shared semantics
Choreography --> EventBus : run-scoped subscribe/publish/cleanup
Orchestration --> Scenario : deterministic outcomes
Choreography --> Scenario : deterministic outcomes
Services --> Persistence : create/retrieve run
Orchestration --> Persistence : persist before advancement
Choreography --> Persistence : persist before event advancement
Persistence --> Database : durable state and ordered trace

note right of EventBus
One controlled advance handler per run.
Deterministic ordered dispatch.
Terminal cleanup / unsubscription.
No broker fallback.
end note

note bottom of Resolver
SUCCESS / FAILURE precedes ALWAYS.
Retry repeats the current task without an edge.
Equal-precedence ambiguity is rejected pre-run.
end note

